{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CexFN5zDkJLAPSNfpqKVG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint for the shipment service. \n\n### Changes Made\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added the `confirm` method that:\n   - Moves a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status\n   - Returns the confirmed shipment\n   - Handles three error cases:\n     - Returns 404 if shipment doesn't exist\n     - Returns 409 with `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` code if shipment is cancelled\n     - Succeeds idempotently if already `CONFIRMED` (no change)\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Added `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` error code to the ErrorCode enum\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 4 comprehensive test cases:\n   - Confirms a CREATED shipment and returns it in CONFIRMED status\n   - Confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing (idempotent)\n   - Rejects confirmation of a CANCELLED shipment with HTTP 409\n   - Rejects confirmation of an unknown shipment with HTTP 404\n\n### Verification\n\n✅ **Build passes**: `./mvnw test` - 17 tests run successfully (5 original + 4 new + 8 other tests)\n✅ **No new dependencies**: pom.xml unchanged\n✅ **Architecture preserved**: Uses existing Kotlin + Spring Boot patterns\n✅ **Error handling**: Consistent with existing API error envelope pattern\n✅ **All criteria met**: Idempotent, cancelled rejection, unknown rejection all working\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":79593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":218},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":